# Windows batch files keep CRLF wherever they are checked out or archived.
#
# Not for a failure that was seen: an LF-only copy of sas4.bat was run on Windows 11 and
# worked, nested for/if blocks and all. The reason is that this repo is downloaded two ways
# -- GitHub's generated source archive, and the release asset built by make_dist.py -- and
# without this the .bat files are the only thing that differs between them. Two downloads
# that are supposed to be the same thing should be the same thing.
*.bat text eol=crlf
